.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt DMA_ALLOC 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm dma_alloc
.Nd allocate device-visible memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn dma_alloc root_dev len align mask_bits flags
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm allocates a physically contiguous, zero-filled buffer a device can reach.
.Fa root_dev
must be the
.Em RootDevice
capability with
.Dv ADMIN
(as for
.Xr mmio_create 2 ) .
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Fa len
is a non-zero multiple of 4096.
.It
.Fa align
is a power of two of at least 4096; 0 means 4096.  The first byte of the
buffer is aligned to it.
.It
.Fa mask_bits
bounds the bus address: every byte of the buffer lies below
.Li 1 << mask_bits .
20..64 are accepted; 0 means 32.
.It
.Fa flags
is 0 or
.Dv NON_CACHEABLE
(1).
.El
The returned handle carries
.Dv READ ,
.Dv WRITE ,
.Dv MAP ,
.Dv DUP
and
.Dv TRANSFER .
It is mapped with
.Xr map 2 :
cached write-back by default (coherent on x86-64) and uncached when the
buffer was created with
.Dv NON_CACHEABLE .
The frames are returned when the last handle closes or the owning process
exits.
.Pp
Each process may hold at most 64 MiB and the whole system at most 25 % of
RAM; further allocations fail with
.Er ENOMEM .
The kernel does not claim DMA isolation:
.Xr dma_info 2
reports the buffer as
.Dv UNPROTECTED
on hardware without an IOMMU.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EPERM
No root capability with
.Dv ADMIN .
.It Er EINVAL
Bad length, alignment, mask or unknown flags.
.It Er ENOMEM
No contiguous range fits the mask, or a budget is exhausted.
.It Er EMFILE
The process handle table is full.
.El
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
